## 🔑 Google Auth + Supabase: No Conflict

> [!NOTE]
> Your desktop currently uses **raw Google OAuth 2.0 with PKCE** (via [googleAuthIpc.js](file:///c:/Projects/Orion%20-%20A%20Multiverse%20of%20Stories/src/main/ipc/googleAuthIpc.js)) to authenticate users and access Google Drive for backup/sync.
>
> **Supabase Auth wraps Google OAuth** — it uses the same Google OAuth flow under the hood but adds:
> - Managed JWT session tokens (no need to handle refresh tokens yourself)
> - A unified user identity (`supabase.auth.user()`) across both platforms
> - Row-Level Security (RLS) on the PostgreSQL database tied to that identity
>
> **Migration path**: Replace the desktop's raw Google OAuth flow with `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({ provider: 'google' })`. The user sees the same "Sign in with Google" button, but auth state is now managed by Supabase. Google Drive features (backup, media locker) can still work — you'd store the Google OAuth access token from Supabase's session and use it for Drive API calls.
>
> **Result**: Same user experience, zero conflict, and both platforms share a single auth identity.

