### Phase 3: Mobile Player & Standalone Streaming

Implement the native media player and the hybrid streaming pipeline.

---

#### Native Player HUD
- `react-native-video` based fullscreen player
- **Gesture zones**: Double-tap seek (±10s left/right), vertical slide brightness (right), vertical slide volume (left)
- **Controls overlay**: Play/pause, seek bar, current time / duration
- **Casting button**: Top-right, opens native AirPlay / Chromecast route picker
- **Sources modal**: Bottom sheet listing available providers with latency indicators
- **Watchdog buffer warning**: Frosted-glass overlay after 15s buffering → "Switch Source" / "Auto Failover"

#### Hybrid Streaming Pipeline
- **Primary (Standalone)**: Hidden `react-native-webview` loads source URLs, injected JS extracts resolved `.m3u8`/`.mp4` stream URLs, feeds them to `react-native-video`
- **Fallback (Desktop Relay)**: When an Orion Desktop node is detected on local Wi-Fi, mobile can delegate scraping to the desktop (desktop resolves the stream, relays the clean URL back over WebSocket)
- **Source failover logic**: Port `getNextHealthyNonAsyncSource` from [registry.js](file:///c:/Projects/Orion%20-%20A%20Multiverse%20of%20Stories/src/renderer/features/player/sources/registry.js#L124-L162) for automatic source switching

